1a:["$","p","p-1",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Long polling"}]," is a request held open until an update or timeout, followed by another request. It can fit environments without a persistent stream, but it still needs timeouts and connection budgets. None of these channels replaces the durable operation record. After reconnect, the client should query current state; an update can be delayed or missed."]}]
1b:["$","h2","h2-1",{"id":"design-a-webhook-as-at-least-once-notification","children":"Design a webhook as at-least-once notification"}]
1c:["$","p","p-2",{"children":["For ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"ExportCompleted"}],", create a webhook delivery record with an event ID and destination. Sign the body using a secret scoped to that endpoint, include a timestamp, enforce a replay window, and validate destination URLs to reduce server-side request forgery risk. Acknowledge a receiver's successful response; retry transient failures with a bounded schedule and show delivery status. Receivers should deduplicate on event ID and respond quickly, handing slow work to their own queue."]}]
1d:["$","p","p-3",{"children":"A webhook should not expose a private download URL to a recipient who lacks access. Include a stable export ID and let the recipient retrieve details through an authorized API."}]
