23:["$","p","p-6",{"children":"A nightly reconciliation job should emit bounded work units, not hold one process open for hours. Give each run a unique ID and each item a stable operation key. If a run overlaps its predecessor, either skip, join, or partition explicitly. Reconciliation can compare accepted exports against completed files and repair a missed outbox publication or status update. Keep the same duplicate-safe worker rule."}]
